module Core

# Each declaration below creates nothing: `@rf` names the shared declaration it shows, and validate-stdlib
# checks that the two still match.

### Represents the protocol for unary bitwise inversion.
### `Invertible` is for values that can flip every bit in their representation
### and return the result as another value of the same type.
@rf("Invertible")
protocol Invertible
    ### Returns the bitwise NOT of this value.
    ### Each bit in the resulting value is the complement of the corresponding bit
    ### in the input.
    ### :returns: The bitwise inverse of this value.
    routine Me.bitnot() -> Me
